# MFlightNaver API

> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.

## Documentation Index
- `SKILL.md` (this file)
- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)
- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)
- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)

## Authentication
Unknown (may need login) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (5)
- `GET /g/100_200/{100_200Token}/NE` — Authenticate using a 100_200 token.
- `GET /g/103_105_201_205/{103_105_201_205Token}/NE` — Authenticate using a 103_105_201_205 token.
- `GET /getLoginStatus` — Check the current login status.
- `GET /international/{internationalToken}/{internationalToken}` — Authenticate using an international token.
- `GET /push/qrcode` — Initiate QR code authentication flow.

### Data Read (4)
- `GET /gfp/v1` — Retrieve flight data using the gfp/v1 endpoint.
- `GET /nac/1` — Retrieve flight data using the nac/1 endpoint.
- `GET /nac/1/{1Id}` — Retrieve flight data using the nac/1/{1Id} endpoint.
- `GET /openrtb/nurl` — Retrieve flight data using the openrtb/nurl endpoint.

### Data Write (4)
- `POST /{id}` — Write data to a specific resource.
- `POST /api/v3/data/` — Write data using the api/v3/data endpoint.
- `POST /sc2/{sc2Id}/` — Write data to a specific sc2 resource.
- `POST /sentry/api/5/envelope/` — Report errors to Sentry.

### Search (1)
- `POST /flight/international/searchFlights` — Search for international flights.

### Config (1)
- `GET /api/runtime-config` — Get runtime configuration for the flight search agent.

## Quick Start

Here are a few examples to get you started with the `m-flight-naver` API:

```typescript
// Example: Retrieving flight data using the gfp/v1 endpoint.
// Assumes necessary parameters are already defined.
async function getFlightData() {
  try {
    const data = await client.gfp_v1();
    console.log("Flight Data:", data);
    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error fetching flight data:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
// Example: Searching for international flights.
// Assumes necessary search parameters (departure, arrival, dates, etc.) are defined.
async function searchInternationalFlights(searchParams: any) {
  try {
    const results = await client.flight_international_searchFlights(searchParams);
    console.log("Search Results:", results);
    return results;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error searching for flights:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

